│  `greeting.py` and `test_greeting.py`. The `greeting.py` file contains a single function `greet(name)` that returns a greeting    │
│  message. The `test_greeting.py` file contains a test function `test_greet()` that tests the `greet()` function.\n\n**Component   │
│  Decomposition**\n\nTo support the requested feature, we will introduce a new component `farewell.py` that will contain the       │
│  `farewell(name)` function. We will also update the `greeting.py` file to include a new function                                  │
│  `farewell(name)`.\n\n**Component Responsibilities**\n\n* `greeting.py`:\n\t+ Contains the `greet(name)` function\n\t+ Contains   │
│  the new `farewell(name)` function\n* `farewell.py`:\n\t+ Contains the new `farewell(name)` function\n* `test_greeting.py`:\n\t+  │
│  Contains the test function `test_greet()` for the `greet()` function\n\t+ Contains a new test function `test_farewell()` for     │
│  the `farewell()` function\n\n**Interfaces between Components**\n\n* `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` will share a common          │
│  interface for the `farewell(name)` function.\n* `test_greeting.py` will interact with both `greeting.py` and `farewell.py`       │
│  through their respective interfaces.\n\n**API Contracts**\n\n* `greeting.py` will expose the `greet(name)` and `farewell(name)`  │
│  functions through its API.\n* `farewell.py` will expose the `farewell(name)` function through its API.\n* `test_greeting.py`     │
│  will interact with the APIs of `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` through their respective interfaces.\n\n**Data Model              │
│  Changes**\n\nNo changes to the data model are required.\n\n**Deployment Topology**\n\nThe repository will be deployed as a       │
│  single unit, with each component (`greeting.py`, `farewell.py`, and `test_greeting.py`) deployed together.\n\n**Security         │
│  Considerations**\n\nNo security considerations are required for this feature.\n\n**Testing Strategy**\n\n* Unit tests will be    │
│  written for each component (`greeting.py`, `farewell.py`, and `test_greeting.py`) to ensure their functionality.\n* Integration  │
│  tests will be written to ensure the components interact correctly.\n\n**Architecture Decisions**\n\n* We will use a modular      │
│  architecture to allow multiple coding workers to implement independent parts of the feature.\n* We will use a shared interface   │
│  for the `farewell(name)` function to allow for easy integration with the `greeting.py` component.\n\n**Risks and                 │
│  Assumptions**\n\n* We assume that the `greeting.py` component is stable and will not be modified during the implementation of    │
│  the `farewell.py` component.\n* We assume that the `test_greeting.py` component will be updated to include tests for the         │
│  `farewell()` function.\n\n**Files/Directories Likely to Change**\n\n* `greeting.py`: updated to include the new                  │
│  `farewell(name)` function\n* `farewell.py`: new file containing the `farewell(name)` function\n* `test_greeting.py`: updated to  │
│  include a new test function `test_farewell()` for the `farewell()` function\n\n**Parallel Implementation Boundaries**\n\nTo      │
│  allow multiple coding workers to implement independent parts of the feature, we will divide the implementation into two          │
│  areas:\n\n* Area 1: `greeting.py` component\n* Area 2: `farewell.py` component and `test_greeting.py` component\n\nEach area     │
│  will be implemented independently, with the `greeting.py` component being updated to include the new `farewell(name)` function,  │
│  and the `farewell.py` component and `test_greeting.py` component being implemented from scratch.\n\n**Implementation             │
│  Plan**\n\n1. Update `greeting.py` to include the new `farewell(name)` function.\n2. Implement `farewell.py` component and        │
│  `test_greeting.py` component independently.\n3. Update `test_greeting.py` to include a new test function `test_farewell()` for   │
│  the `farewell()` function.\n\nBy following this architecture proposal, we can ensure a maintainable and scalable architecture    │
│  for the requested feature.'}                                                                                                     │
