+**Architecture Proposal**
+
+**Existing System Analysis**
+
+The existing repository consists of two files: `greeting.py` and `test_greeting.py`. The `greeting.py` file contains a single function `greet(name)` that returns a greeting message. The `test_greeting.py` file contains a test function `test_greet()` that tests the `greet()` function.
+
+**Component Decomposition**
+
+To support the requested feature, we will introduce a new component `farewell.py` that will contain the `farewell(name)` function. We will also update the `greeting.py` file to include a new function `farewell(name)`.
+
+**Component Responsibilities**
+
+* `greeting.py`:
+	+ Contains the `greet(name)` function
+	+ Contains the new `farewell(name)` function
+* `farewell.py`:
+	+ Contains the new `farewell(name)` function
+* `test_greeting.py`:
+	+ Contains the test function `test_greet()` for the `greet()` function
+	+ Contains a new test function `test_farewell()` for the `farewell()` function
+
+**Interfaces between Components**
+
+* `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` will share a common interface for the `farewell(name)` function.
+* `test_greeting.py` will interact with both `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` through their respective interfaces.
+
+**API Contracts**
+
+* `greeting.py` will expose the `greet(name)` and `farewell(name)` functions through its API.
+* `farewell.py` will expose the `farewell(name)` function through its API.
+* `test_greeting.py` will interact with the APIs of `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` through their respective interfaces.
+
+**Data Model Changes**
+
+No changes to the data model are required.
+
+**Deployment Topology**
+
+The repository will be deployed as a single unit, with each component (`greeting.py`, `farewell.py`, and `test_greeting.py`) deployed together.
+
+**Security Considerations**
+
+No security considerations are required for this feature.
+
+**Testing Strategy**
