+**README**
+
+Welcome to the Greeting and Farewell System!
+
+This system provides a simple way to generate greetings and farewells for users. It consists of two main components: `greeting.py` and `farewell.py`. The `greeting.py` component contains a function `greet(name)` that returns a greeting message, while the `farewell.py` component contains a function `farewell(name)` that returns a farewell message.
+
+**Installation**
+
+To install the system, simply clone the repository and run the following commands:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/your-username/greeting-and-farewell-system.git
+cd greeting-and-farewell-system
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
+
+**Configuration**
+
+The system does not require any configuration. However, you can customize the greeting and farewell messages by modifying the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` files.
+
+**Environment Variables**
+
+The system does not use any environment variables.
+
+**API Usage**
+
+The system provides two APIs:
+
+* `greet(name)`: Returns a greeting message for the given name.
+* `farewell(name)`: Returns a farewell message for the given name.
+
+You can use these APIs by importing the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` modules and calling the `greet()` and `farewell()` functions.
+
+**Architecture**
+
+The system consists of two main components: `greeting.py` and `farewell.py`. The `greeting.py` component contains a function `greet(name)` that returns a greeting message, while the `farewell.py` component contains a function `farewell(name)` that returns a farewell message.
+
+The system uses a modular architecture to allow for easy extension and modification of the components.
+
+**Operational Runbook**
+
+To run the system, simply execute the following commands:
+
+```bash
+python greeting.py
+python farewell.py
+```
+
+This will generate the greeting and farewell messages for the given names.
+
+**Troubleshooting**
+
+If you encounter any issues with the system, you can try the following:
+
+* Check the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` files for any syntax errors.
+* Make sure that the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` files are in the same directory as the `test_greeting.py` file.
+* Try running the system in debug mode by adding the `--debug` flag to the command.
+
+**Deployment**
+
+To deploy the system, simply clone the repository and run the following commands:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/your-username/greeting-and-farewell-system.git
+cd greeting-and-farewell-system
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
+
+You can then deploy the system to your production environment by copying the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` files to the desired location.
+
+**Known Limitations**
+
+The system has the following known limitations:
+
+* The system only generates greeting and farewell messages for a single name.
+* The system does not support multiple languages.
+* The system does not have any error handling mechanisms.
+
+**API Documentation**
+
+### Greeting API
+
+#### greet(name)
+
+Returns a greeting message for the given name.
+
+* **Parameters:**
+	+ `name`: The name to generate a greeting for.
+* **Returns:**
+	+ A greeting message for the given name.
+
+### Farewell API
+
+#### farewell(name)
+
+Returns a farewell message for the given name.
+
+* **Parameters:**
+	+ `name`: The name to generate a farewell for.
+* **Returns:**
+	+ A farewell message for the given name.
+
+**Configuration Documentation**
+
+The system does not require any configuration. However, you can customize the greeting and farewell messages by modifying the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` files.
+
+**Environment Variables Documentation**
+
+The system does not use any environment variables.
+
+**Architecture Documentation**
+
+The system consists of two main components: `greeting.py` and `farewell.py`. The `greeting.py` component contains a function `greet(name)` that returns a greeting message, while the `farewell.py` component contains a function `farewell(name)` that returns a farewell message.
+
+The system uses a modular architecture to allow for easy extension and modification of the components.
+
+**Runbook Documentation**
+
+To run the system, simply execute the following commands:
+
+```bash
+python greeting.py
+python farewell.py
+```
+
+This will generate the greeting and farewell messages for the given names.
+
+**Troubleshooting Documentation**
+
+If you encounter any issues with the system, you can try the following:
+
+* Check the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` files for any syntax errors.
+* Make sure that the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` files are in the same directory as the `test_greeting.py` file.
+* Try running the system in debug mode by adding the `--debug` flag to the command.
+
+**Deployment Documentation**
+
+To deploy the system, simply clone the repository and run the following commands:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/your-username/greeting-and-farewell-system.git
+cd greeting-and-farewell-system
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
+
+You can then deploy the system to your production environment by copying the `greeting.py` and `farewell.py` files to the desired location.
+
+**Known Limitations Documentation**
+
+The system has the following known limitations:
+
+* The system only generates greeting and farewell messages for a single name.
+* The system does not support multiple languages.
+* The system does not have any error handling mechanisms.
